Enumeration is the act to identifying all of the ways we could attack a target we must find.
We need to know what to do with the information we get from them tools are just tools.
It is essential to know how they work and what syntax they use 
Two points:
-Functions and/or resources that allow us to interact with the tharget and/or provide additional information.
-Information that provides us with even more important information to acces our target.
Most scanning tools use a timeout while waiting to receive a response from a service/port. 
If this service/port does not respond within a specific amount of time, the tool will mark it as closed, filtered, or unknown.
In the last two cases, we will still be able to work with it.
However, if a port is marked as closed and Nmap doesn't show it to us, we will be in a bad situation.
This service/port may provide us with an opportunity to find a way to access the system. Therefore, this can cost us a lot of unnecessary time before we find it.

